From 02bb1bbfb49ed66389d1931e335461b474ebb70d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:14:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 123/125] net: sparx5: add LAG offload

A bond in a bridge does not forward on LAN969x.  The driver does not
offload link aggregation, so the bond is a software port in an
offloaded bridge, and the switch never hands its traffic to the CPU:
unknown unicast from the other bridge ports stays in hardware, and
frames for the bridge arriving on the bond members are dropped.

Offload the bond instead.  Ports enslaved to a bond join the bridge
through it, the bond's members share an aggregation mask and a logical
port, MAC table entries for the bond point to its lowest numbered
member, and frames are not sent back out the aggregate they came in on.
MDB entries and VLANs on the bond are applied to each member, and FDB
entries for foreign bridge ports are installed towards the CPU.

Based on the LAG support by Daniel Machon in Microchip's BSP kernel,
branch bsp-6.12-2025:

  commit 5fd9c90023a0 ("net: sparx5/lan969x: add registers required to configure LAG")
  commit 684893932384 ("net: sparx5/lan969x: expose sparx5_mac_entry struct")
  commit 9b7df456732a ("net: sparx5/lan969x: pass sparx5_port in sparx5_fdb_call_notifiers()")
  commit 5e7ca258ec39 ("net: sparx5/lan969x: add function to set the destination PGID's")
  commit 33d523ead729 ("net: sparx5/lan969x: use switchdev_handle_fdb_event_to_device helper")
  commit 94f4b8667c48 ("net: sparx5/lan969x: move unoffloading to PRECHANGEUPPER")
  commit 5baa99df9a9d ("net: sparx5/lan969x: add new brport_dev argument")
  commit 9cfbe0dee25d ("net: sparx5/lan969x: add LAG support")
  commit d17f1c4c4bce ("net: sparx5/lan969x: do not send frames back on LAG ports")
  commit 64054ae42e82 ("net: sparx5: handle foreign device FDB events")
  commit c92187b2b2a5 ("net: sparx5: allow foreign devices in bridge")

and the MDB fix for LAG interfaces by Horatiu Vultur:

  commit 7beaccf08da5 ("net: sparx5: Fix for MDB")

Adapted to the mainline 6.18 driver: registers in its regs->gaddr form,
with ANA_CL_PORT_ID_CFG added, the source and destination masks folded
into sparx5_update_fwd(), the MDB fix applied to the MDB code in
sparx5_switchdev.c, and the HSR, MRP, XDP and QoS parts of those
commits left out.  Switchdev attributes of the bond are accepted on its
member ports, and the bridge's own addresses are still installed for the
CPU when the bridge gets them before any port joins, as before the
switch to switchdev_handle_fdb_event_to_device().

Signed-off-by: Daniel Machon <daniel.machon@microchip.com>
Signed-off-by: Horatiu Vultur <horatiu.vultur@microchip.com>
Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
